   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch8/q1",
   "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:35mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch8/q01-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 3: a pendulum hanging from a fixed point, displaced by an angle θ from the dashed downward vertical, with a dashed arc showing its swing\"></figure><p>The motion of a pendulum, shown in Figure 3, is modelled by the differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm d^2\\theta}{\\mathrm dt^2}+9\\theta=\\frac12\\cos3t\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> is the angle, in radians, that the pendulum makes with the downward vertical, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds after it begins to move.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><p>Show that a particular solution of the differential equation is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac{1}{12}t\\sin3t\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence, find the general solution of the differential equation. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol></li></ol><p>Initially, the pendulum</p><ul><li>makes an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\"></span> radians with the downward vertical</li><li>is at rest</li></ul><p>Given that, 10 seconds after it begins to move, the pendulum makes an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> radians with the downward vertical,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>determine, according to the model, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the true value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> is 0.62</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li>evaluate the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>The differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm d^2\\theta}{\\mathrm dt^2}+9\\theta=\\frac12\\cos3t\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>models the motion of the pendulum as moving with forced harmonic motion.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"4\"><li>Refine the differential equation so that the motion of the pendulum is simple harmonic motion. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
